    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "info_section",
      "content": "## Viscosity Information\n\n**Viscosity** is a measure of a fluid's resistance to gradual deformation by shear stress or tensile stress.\n\n### Dynamic Viscosity Output Units:\n- Pa·s (Pascal seconds)\n- cP (centipoise)\n- mPa·s (millipascal seconds)\n- lbf·s/ft² (pound-force seconds per square foot)\n- lbm/ft·h (pound-mass per foot-hour)\n\n### Kinematic Viscosity Output Units:\n- cSt (centistoke)\n- m²/s (square meters per second)\n- ft²/s (square feet per second)\n\n### Unit Conversion:\n- 1 cP = 0.001 Pa·s = 0.01 P\n- 1 Pa·s = 1000 cP = 10 P\n- 1 cSt = 1 mm²/s = 1×10⁻⁶ m²/s\n- 1 m²/s = 1×10⁶ cSt"
    }
